  "details": "Introduced: 1 December 2021 [7809310]\n(it worked as of 18 November 2021 [7738952])\nSetting the hip's tracking to Animation used to make it be where the animation tells it to be. This is no longer the case, now it still tracks to be under the head (as if it was set to Tracking)\nTested with avatar that was uploaded way before the offending build was released.\nConfirmed broken on Windows 10 with Valve Index (VR), and on Ubuntu with Proton (Desktop)\nGallery:\nhttps://i.imgur.com/G5l2YLz.jpg\nSitting animation not working as intended.\nhttps://i.imgur.com/or8IdfS.jpg\nEnvironment hidden, showing that the hip is underground, not on the floor as the animation would instruct.\nhttps://i.imgur.com/sX1wZAB.jpg\nThe debug menu shows that hip tracking is indeed disabled. The feet work fine, though.\n\nUpdate:\nDowngrading the client by manually downloading 18 November 2021's manifest shows that the issue did not exist before the aforementioned build: https://i.imgur.com/oiu1Bll.jpg (same avatar, hip working as intended)",
